\tag{fdip}
\title{Spectral action as induced action}
\date{2026-11-03}

\p{Can a gauge weight be read from the spectrum of an operator that the
graph already determines, rather than supplied as a face term?}

\p{On a triangle-free graph, the gauge-dependent part of the fourth
power of the massless covariant Laplacian is eight times a sum over 4-cycles.
The following section proves that identity and says when those cycles
are the plaquettes of a square torus. A comparison with the logarithm
of the massive precision, and with a continuum limit cited in that
section, remains speculative.}

\transclude{fdip-00A7}
